1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:09,006
Welcome to the demonstration of the Bachat Gat Digital Savings Group Management System.

2
00:00:09,006 --> 00:00:12,526
We begin at the secure admin authentication portal.

3
00:00:12,526 --> 00:00:23,088
Role-based access control ensures that only authorized administrators can access group accounts, record transactions, and manage microfinance operations.

4
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:35,640
Here on the Real-Time Dashboard, administrators get a transparent overview of the group's financial standing.

5
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:39,426
At the top, you can see our isolated test group badge.

6
00:00:39,426 --> 00:00:49,309
The fundamental accounting equation is highlighted here: Total Group Fund equals Available Cash Balance in bank plus Active Loan Outstanding.

7
00:00:49,309 --> 00:00:52,744
Every rupee collected is reconciled in real time.

8
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,643
Next, we navigate to Member Management.

9
00:01:05,643 --> 00:01:11,471
A key architectural principle of our system is mutually exclusive member partitioning.

10
00:01:11,471 --> 00:01:20,417
Members are categorized into Active Loan Members who are repaying installments, and Non-Loan Members who contribute regular savings.

11
00:01:20,417 --> 00:01:24,144
The real-time search allows quick lookup of any member.

12
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:33,537
For an Active Loan Member with an active ₹5,000 loan, only 'Record Loan Payment' is enabled.

13
00:01:33,537 --> 00:01:41,496
Standalone savings is disabled because savings are collected with loan installments, ensuring atomic accounting.

14
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:49,540
Clicking into the member's profile opens a 360-degree audit view.

15
00:01:49,540 --> 00:02:02,952
Here, the system maintains a complete lifetime ledger showing cumulative monthly savings, active and closed loans, and an immutable repayment transaction log for total individual transparency.

16
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,840
Returning to the directory, we inspect a Non-Loan Member.

17
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:13,016
Members without active debt display the green 'No Loan' badge.

18
00:02:13,016 --> 00:02:20,696
For these members, the standalone 'Record Savings' button is active, set to the standardized ₹1,000 monthly share.

19
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:35,989
Opening the Record Savings modal reveals an essential accounting distinction: the Scheduled Month and Year represent the accounting accrual period, while the Payment Date tracks actual cash inflow.

20
00:02:35,989 --> 00:02:41,528
The modal supports Cash, UPI, and Bank transfers, maintaining complete UI stability.

21
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:51,770
In the Savings Ledger section, the system logs every monthly contribution.

22
00:02:51,770 --> 00:03:02,600
To protect data integrity, strict unique constraints prevent duplicate savings entries for the same member within the same month, eliminating accidental double-entries.

23
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:12,852
Moving to Loans and Repayments, we see the micro-lending portfolio.

24
00:03:12,852 --> 00:03:20,745
Each loan card displays key terms: Principal of ₹5,000, 2% monthly interest, and a 10-month installment term.

25
00:03:20,745 --> 00:03:24,872
Clicking 'View Details' opens the comprehensive schedule.

26
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:32,328
On the Loan Details page, the system presents an automated 10-month amortization schedule.

27
00:03:32,328 --> 00:03:38,727
The system uses reducing-balance interest calculated strictly at 2% on remaining principal.

28
00:03:38,727 --> 00:03:44,000
As principal is repaid, the monthly interest charge reduces proportionally.

29
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:58,700
We execute a live repayment for Installment Number One: ₹500 principal plus ₹100 reducing interest at 2%, totaling ₹600 cash.

30
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:08,544
Upon submission, outstanding principal immediately updates from ₹5,000 to ₹4,500, reflected across the loan ledger.

31
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:31,303
Navigating to Reports, we examine the Pending Dues tab.

32
00:04:31,303 --> 00:04:42,648
For September 2026, the loan issue month has zero installments due, and all member savings are fully paid, displaying exact zero pending arrears.

33
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:50,813
Switching to the Loans Overview tab, we review macro lending analytics.

34
00:04:50,813 --> 00:05:01,456
Administrators can track total deployed capital, cumulative interest earnings, overall recovery velocity, and the group's active credit exposure at a glance.

35
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:11,632
The cornerstone of Bachat Gat auditing is the Monthly Balance Report, known traditionally as Taaleband.

36
00:05:11,632 --> 00:05:22,256
Our system enforces strict column separation: Regular Savings, Loan Principal, and Interest Earnings are tracked in mutually exclusive columns with zero commingling.

37
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:39,200
Returning to the dashboard, we confirm reconciliation: Available Cash of ₹15,600 plus Active Loans of ₹4,500 matches Total Group Fund of ₹20,100 with zero variance.

38
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:50,773
In conclusion, the Bachat Gat platform delivers robust microfinance management, automated lending, and strict Taaleband reconciliation.

39
00:05:50,773 --> 00:05:51,460
Thank you.

